? Which description best defines multimedia?
+ Combining digital text, graphics, sound, animation or video
- Storing every document as an unformatted text file
- Sending only printed messages to a large audience
- Processing numerical data without presenting information
= Multimedia combines media elements to communicate through electronic devices.

? Which feature makes a multimedia learning title interactive?
+ The learner chooses which explanation to open next
- The video contains both speech and moving pictures
- The title is stored on a computer hard disk
- The presentation uses a high-resolution photograph
= Interactivity concerns user control over what is presented and when.

? A museum map links to photographs, narration and videos. What is this linked structure called?
+ Hypermedia
- Plain text
- Notation
- Encoding
= Hypermedia connects different media types through navigable links.

? How should a camera photograph be classified by origin and time property?
+ Captured and discrete
- Captured and continuous
- Synthesized and discrete
- Synthesized and continuous
= The camera captures a real scene, and the still image has no intrinsic time sequence.

? How should computer-generated animation be classified?
+ Synthesized and continuous
- Captured and continuous
- Synthesized and discrete
- Captured and discrete
= A computer generates it, and its movement depends on a sequence over time.

? A lesson lets students choose a topic freely but requires ordered steps inside each demonstration. Which organisation fits best?
+ Composite structure
- Strictly linear structure
- Unconnected file structure
- Single-level static structure
= Composite organisation combines free navigation with constrained linear sequences.

? Which information organisation arranges content as parent and child branches?
+ Hierarchical
- Continuous
- Captured
- Temporal
= Hierarchical organisation forms a tree, such as home → subjects → lessons.

? In the three-layer multimedia model, where do operating systems, communication systems and databases belong?
+ System layer
- Device layer
- Application layer
- Presentation content
= The system layer supplies shared services used by applications and devices.

? What is the main purpose of a multimedia authoring tool?
+ Integrating assets with timing, navigation and interaction
- Capturing only pressure changes from a microphone
- Replacing every media asset with a printed document
- Supplying electrical power to physical input devices
= Authoring coordinates prepared assets into a functioning multimedia title.

? Which communication pattern is characteristic of new media in the lesson?
+ Many participants produce, receive and respond
- One broadcaster sends without audience feedback
- Only printers distribute fixed paper documents
- No participant can create or modify content
= New media support many-to-many interaction and content contribution.

? Which problem is especially important for continuous multimedia?
+ Maintaining timing and synchronisation during playback
- Keeping every still image in alphabetic order
- Ensuring all characters use decorative typefaces
- Removing every choice from the user interface
= Sound, moving pictures and animation depend on timely delivery; related media must stay aligned.

? Which item is part of the PDF's user perspective for evaluating a multimedia title?
+ Platform compatibility
- Production-team hierarchy
- Source-code naming style
- Developer office location
= Users consider relevant content, platform compatibility, usability and cost.

? A home-shaped control clearly suggests returning to the first screen. Which property does this illustrate?
+ Intuitive interface
- Continuous origin
- Synthesized capture
- Nonlinear encoding
= An intuitive control gives an understandable clue about its function.

? A student replays an explanation before moving forward. Which multimedia benefit is most directly illustrated?
+ Self-paced learning
- Fixed broadcast scheduling
- Higher storage consumption
- One-way mass distribution
= Self-paced interaction allows learners to process material at their own speed.
